          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            be (usually
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+category"} strict
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mo
                                %mi u
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇙
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ↓
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mo
                                %mi v
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  A
                  \&amp;
                  \\overset{f}{\longrightarrow}
                  \&amp;
                  B
                  \\\
                  \\mathllap{^u}
                  \\Big\downarrow
                  \&amp; \swArrow &amp;
                  \\Big\downarrow
                  \\mathrlap{^v}
                  \\\
                  C
                  \&amp;\underset{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  D
                  }
          %p
            that is filled by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            (which might be an
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+natural+transformation"} identity
          %p
            This is said to be an
            %strong exact square
            if the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck-Chevalley+transformation"} Beck-Chevalley transformation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi u
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mo !
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_! f^* \to g^* v_!,
          %p
            relating functors with values in some other category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*\colon M^B\to M^A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^*\colon M^D\to M^C
            denote precomposition with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            respectively, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi u
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_!\colon M^A\to M^C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_!\colon M^B\to M^D
            denote pointwise left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extensions"} Kan extensions
            along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi u
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi u
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi v
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi u
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi u
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  u_! f^*
                  \\longrightarrow
                  u_! f^* v^* v_!
                  \\longrightarrow
                  u_! u^* g^* v_!
                  \\longrightarrow
                  g^* v_!
          %p
            of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+an+adjunction"}> co
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
            maps.
          %p
            By the general calculus of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mates"} mates
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi v
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi u
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v^* g_* \to f_* u^*
          %p
            is an isomorphism, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_*
            denote pointwise
            %em right
            Kan extensions.
          %p
            This definition refers to Kan extensions of diagrams with values in any category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            (whenever such Kan extensions exist). If a square is exact only relative to diagrams defined in a
            %em particular
            category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                \-exact
          %p This is a “functional” definition, which generalizes correctly to other contexts (see below). However, in the case of ordinary categories and Kan extensions, there is a precise combinatorial characterization of which squares are exact. Thus, when using exactness to compute with Kan extensions in practice, we can use the combinatorial characterization to verify that a square is exact, then apply the definition above to compute one Kan extension in terms of another.
          %h2#generalizations Generalizations
          %h3#in_2categories In 2-categories
          %p
            The definition given above generalizes directly to squares inhabited by a 2-cell in any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
          %ul
            %li
              Internal
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointwise+Kan+extension"} pointwise Kan extension
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              with finite
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limits"} 2-limits
            %li
              Enriched pointwise Kan extensions in a 2-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V Cat
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V Cat
              %a{:href => "Kan+extension#In2cat"} here
              for a counterexample.
            %li
              Pointwise Kan extensions can also be defined in any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+structure"} Yoneda structure
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category+equipped+with+proarrows"} 2-category equipped with proarrows
            %li
              In the world of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} (infinity,1)-categories
              we have a notion of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+exact+square"} homotopy exact square
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivators"} derivators
          %p The combinatorial characterization of exact squares has a corresponding version for any of these generalizations, although in different cases it will be more or less explicit.
          %h3#in_double_categories In double categories
          %p
